# Files Cloud Build should NOT upload as part of `gcloud run deploy --source .`
#
# Strategy: mirror .gitignore + add a couple of cloud-specific exclusions.
# The control-plane image (see Dockerfile) only needs control/, web/static/,
# requirements-control.txt, and per-channel config.yaml + uploads/ +
# narrations/ + raw/. Everything else is dead weight in the build context.

# === Python / venvs (huge) ===
.venv/
.venv-*/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# === Env / secrets ===
.env
.agent-token

# === OS / IDE ===
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
.git/

# === Build artifacts ===
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
node_modules/
dist/
build/

# === Model weights ===
*.onnx
*.bin
*.safetensors
*.pt
*.ckpt

# === Heavy regenerable per-channel dirs ===
# Footage source mp4s — biggest offender (10+ GB on historyrecapped).
# The cloud has no use for these; render workers download fresh.
**/footage/
**/cache/
**/scratch/
**/emoji/
**/tts_tests/
**/cooking_loops/
**/critiques/
**/branding/*.png
**/branding/*.jpg
**/songs/
**/shorts/*.mp4

# Heavy media in narrations/ (the .json files we DO want; .wav we don't).
**/narrations/*.wav
**/narrations/*.mp3

# === Per-slug regenerables (LLM-authored, regen in seconds) ===
**/cast/**/*.json
**/prompts/**/*.json
**/dossier/**/*.json
**/shotlist/**/*.json
**/footage/transcripts/**/*.json
**/specs/**/*.yaml

# === Cross-channel runtime / scratch state ===
data/_jobs/
data/telemetry/
data/cache/
data/scratch/
data/intermediate/
data/research/youtube/

# === Logs / temp ===
*.log
*.tmp
.tmp/
*.bak
*~

# === Docs / screenshots / large image assets ===
docs/screenshots/
docs/diagrams/*.png
